    "id": "ocean-ts-diagram",
    "title": "Temperature–Salinity (T–S) Diagram",
    "field": "Oceanography / Limnology",
    "plotType": "Scatter of paired T & S samples with density (σ_t) isopycnals",
    "description": "Each point is one paired temperature and salinity measurement from a cast, plotted with salinity on the x-axis and temperature on the y-axis. Curved background contours are lines of constant density (σ_t isopycnals). Distinct water masses appear as tight clusters, and mixing between them falls along straight lines connecting the clusters.",
    "dataNeeded": [
      {
        "name": "Water temperature",
        "unit": "°C"
      },
      {
        "name": "Salinity",
        "unit": "PSU"
      }
    ],
    "whatItTellsYou": "How many distinct water masses are present, their characteristic T–S signatures, and how they mix. Because it removes depth, it exposes water-mass identity and stability directly: points crossing to denser isopycnals (down-right) are heavier, and a straight run of points between two clusters is a mixing line, not a new mass.",
